This repository contains original scripts, measurements and documentation.

It does NOT redistribute any upstream source and does NOT contain model weights.
`patches/fix_transformers_weightmap.py` is an original script that edits a local copy of a
transformers file to correct an upstream bug; the transformers source itself is not
included here.

Upstream projects referenced:
  vLLM                              Apache-2.0   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
  llm-compressor                    Apache-2.0   https://github.com/vllm-project/llm-compressor
  compressed-tensors                Apache-2.0   https://github.com/neuralmagic/compressed-tensors
  transformers                      Apache-2.0   https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
  Qwen3.8-27B                       Apache-2.0   see model card on HuggingFace (Qwen)
  Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored            Apache-2.0   see model card on HuggingFace
                                    (JonathanColetti); abliterated with Heretic
                                    (https://github.com/p-e-w/heretic), then published as
                                    bf16 and GGUF
  wikitext-2-raw-v1                 CC BY-SA 3.0 Salesforce/wikitext, used as calibration
                                    and perplexity corpus only

The quantization recipe in `scripts/quantize_v3.py` reproduces the structure of the
quantization_config published in an existing NVFP4 build of Qwen3.8-27B. Configuration
values are facts about a published artifact, not copied source.

The referenced checkpoint is an abliterated (refusal-removed) model. This repository
documents quantization, serving configuration and performance/accuracy measurement only.
It is published to support authorized security testing, red-team evaluation and
refusal-mechanism research in isolated environments, and contains no harmful content,
jailbreak material, or capability demonstrations. Anyone deploying such a checkpoint is
responsible for providing independent safety and moderation layers; the upstream card
states that refusal behaviour is substantially reduced, not eliminated.

No retraining, fine-tuning, GPTQ or AWQ was performed. Weights are converted by
round-to-nearest into the FP4/FP8 grids. Calibration consists of forward passes only and
never modifies a weight; it exists solely to observe activation ranges for the FP4
activation global scales and the static FP8 KV-cache scales, neither of which can be
derived from weights.

Benchmark numbers were measured on the author's own hardware and are reported as measured,
including the runs that failed, the hypotheses that turned out to be wrong, and the build
that passed needle-retrieval while being 6% worse in perplexity.
